WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.759
An alarm informs someone of a condition;

2
00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:06.189
an interlock can inhibit or change an
operation.

3
00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:10.516
A warning on the display does not prove a
heater has stopped.

4
00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:15.050
The fictional requirement must state which
outputs are expected.

5
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:19.101
Observe the relevant physical or defined
simulated output

6
00:00:19.221 --> 00:00:21.979
rather than relying on the screen alone.

7
00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:25.841
Identify where the challenge enters the
system.

8
00:00:25.961 --> 00:00:30.270
A simulated transmitter signal can
exercise downstream logic

9
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.873
while excluding the sensing element.

10
00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:36.786
A controller status bit may exclude the
final actuator.

11
00:00:36.906 --> 00:00:40.148
Combine complementary evidence where
justified,

12
00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.750
and describe each boundary honestly.

13
00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.491
Do not label a partial simulation as a
complete physical loop test.

14
00:00:48.111 --> 00:00:50.111
Test the specified reset

15
00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:53.610
and restart behavior as well as the
initial trip.

16
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:58.282
Removing a fault does not necessarily
authorize automatic restart.

17
00:00:58.402 --> 00:01:00.402
For this fictional case,

18
00:01:00.522 --> 00:01:03.626
manual reset is a stated teaching
assumption.

19
00:01:03.746 --> 00:01:07.677
The actual requirement must come from the
approved design

20
00:01:07.797 --> 00:01:12.762
and risk assessment, with any stored alarm
history retained as required.

21
00:01:13.382 --> 00:01:16.141
Record the alarm and protective response

22
00:01:16.261 --> 00:01:18.882
separately, including relevant timing.

23
00:01:19.001 --> 00:01:21.898
If the alarm appears but the output fails,

24
00:01:22.018 --> 00:01:24.777
the combined requirement has not passed.

25
00:01:24.897 --> 00:01:28.630
Preserve both observations and assess the
discrepancy.

26
00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.543
An attractive screenshot of the warning
does not repair

27
00:01:32.663 --> 00:01:36.180
missing evidence of the required
protective action.
